{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scvi_n200 dramatically outperforms pca_n2000 for RNA encoding (0.6776 vs ~0.635-0.639), and avgpool aggregation is clearly superior to transformer (0.635-0.678 vs 0.573). The best configuration (config_038: scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted) achieved 0.6776 at a modest 5.90 GPU hours. The key remaining uncertainty is whether the larger imagenet_vit_l image encoder can further boost performance when paired with the superior scvi_n200 RNA encoder. config_001 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) is the most direct exploitation of the winning direction, testing only the image encoder swap. With pca_n2000, ViT-L and ResNet50 were nearly tied (0.635 vs 0.639), but with a stronger RNA branch, the richer image features from ViT-L may provide a larger complementary signal. Expected cost is moderate (~7-8 GPU hours), comparable to config_004, since ViT-L is the main cost driver and scvi_n200 is cheaper than pca_n2000. This is the highest-value next experiment: it either confirms resnet50 is sufficient (saving budget) or reveals a new best configuration to build upon in the remaining 5 experiments."
}

